course: dictionary
lesson: 3055
title: Odd, but harmless: the word eccentric
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An eccentric person does things in an unusual, strange way, but the way is usually harmless. Nobody is hurt. «She is an eccentric old lady who keeps forty cats and paints her front door purple.» The clues are the forty cats and the purple door: they are odd, but no one is in danger, so eccentric means odd but friendly.
explain: Look for clues that show whether the strangeness is harmful. «The eccentric inventor wore a hat made of spoons and tinkered with clocks all night.» Spoon hats and night-time tinkering are odd, but they are not dangerous. If the sentence showed cruelty or danger, a different word would fit better.
explain: Eccentric can also be a noun: an eccentric is such a person. Phrases help too: «a bit eccentric» means slightly odd, and «an eccentric old man» means an odd old man. Use the swap check: put "odd but harmless" into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: In maths and science, eccentric means not centred. An eccentric circle or orbit is one that is not around a central middle point, or an oval path. It is the same word with a different job, and the link is the idea of not sitting in the middle.
fact: Eccentric is an adjective, and an eccentric is a noun for such a person.
fact: «Eccentric» means odd or strange in a harmless way.
fact: «A bit eccentric» means slightly odd.
fact: In maths and science, eccentric means not centred, like an oval path.
fact: Eccentric is a polite word: it describes odd people without being rude.
exercise: «The eccentric inventor wore a hat made of spoons.» What does eccentric mean here? | Dangerous and cruel | *Odd in a harmless way | Lost and afraid | Very rich and famous
exercise: Which word is a polite way to describe a person who is odd in a harmless way? | famished | curt | glum | *eccentric
exercise: «She is a bit eccentric.» What does «a bit eccentric» suggest? | Very dangerous | *Slightly odd | Extremely wealthy | Completely silent
test: «Eccentric» in maths means: | Very hungry | Short and rude | Glowing with light | *Not centred, like an oval path
test: In «Grandad is an eccentric who keeps rubber ducks in every room», what kind of word is eccentric? | *Noun | Verb | Adverb | Adjective
exam: Which word best fits the meaning of eccentric in «an eccentric old man who painted his shed purple»? | Dangerous | Silent | Hungry | *Odd but harmless
